%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Gibbon
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 13
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Port Line
    AbilityDescription: 'The LEFT trigger. Hold it and a beam winds up along the hull''s
      own left-hand axis - the analog depth IS the distance, drawn ahead of you as you
      squeeze. Let go and the beam fires: it cuts every hostile prism on its path and
      plants an anchor prism of your own domain at its endpoint, which the line then
      swings you around. Press again to drop the line and start winding the next shot
      in the same motion - one squeeze per arm is the whole rhythm. Charge scales the
      beam''s CUT: reach is Space''s job, this is how much the beam can sever on the way
      out. Authored on GibbonTetherConfigSO.BeamCutRadius, so the generic map multiplier
      stays 1.0 (no double-dip). NOTE the two arms are mechanically IDENTICAL - the beam
      direction is the only difference - so this entry and Mass''s differ in side and in
      nothing else.'
    Input: 2
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: ''
    UpgradeDescription: 'OPEN DESIGN SLOT - not authored, deliberately. The two arms are
      symmetric, so an upgrade here has to be either arm-agnostic (in which case it
      belongs on whichever element owns the mechanic, not on one arm) or an asymmetry
      between left and right that nobody has designed yet. Left empty so the ability row
      reports it LOCKED rather than green.'
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Starboard Line
    AbilityDescription: 'The RIGHT trigger. Identical to Port Line but fired along the
      hull''s right-hand axis. Because the beams are locked to the HULL''S lateral axis
      and never to a reticle, ROLL is this vessel''s aiming control: bank ninety degrees
      and the right trigger fires straight up. Two sticks fly the ship and the ship aims
      the beams, which is what makes this a two-thumb flyer rather than a cursor game.
      Mass scales the ANCHOR the beam plants (GibbonTetherConfigSO.AnchorScale) - a bigger
      anchor is more conserved mass left in the arena and a wider thing to swing on.'
    Input: 1
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: ''
    UpgradeDescription: 'OPEN DESIGN SLOT - see Port Line. Not authored.'
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: (open design slot)
    AbilityDescription: 'NOT AUTHORED. The natural home, once the vessel has been flown,
      is REACH - MaxBeamLength and BeamTravelSpeed - which is exactly the fleet''s Space
      convention and is also the strategically loaded number here: beam length sets the
      angular momentum you bank when the line goes taut, and the swing tops out near
      sqrt(L*w), so a longer beam literally pays out more speed. Recorded as a proposal
      in Docs/ElementalAbilitySystem/FLEET_MAPS.md, not implemented, pending sign-off.'
    Input: 0
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: ''
    UpgradeDescription: ''
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: (open design slot)
    AbilityDescription: 'NOT AUTHORED. The natural home is the SWING''s rate - ReelRate
      and MaxSwingRate - which is the fleet''s Time convention (rate/mobility) and is the
      vessel''s only accelerator. Recorded as a proposal in FLEET_MAPS.md, not
      implemented, pending sign-off.'
    Input: 0
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: ''
    UpgradeDescription: ''
